 "notes": "CardDemo's pending-authorization summary screen (transaction CPVS, program COPAUS0C, app-authorization-ims-db2-mq): pseudo-conversational. Given an account it reads the card cross-reference (through the CXACAIX alternate index), the account and the customer, schedules PSB PSBPAUTB (EXEC DLI SCHD), reads the account's PAUTSUM0 summary segment (GU qualified by ACCNTID) and lists its PAUTDTL1 details five to a page (GNP, a sixth probes for a next page); PF8 / PF7 page forward and back by repositioning (GNP WHERE the page's key), an 'S' beside a row XCTLs to COPAUS1C, PF3 XCTLs to the caller. The PSB is released by SYNCPOINT before each SEND. The database is the corpus's own HD unload (22 roots, the last with a blank key left out), the VSAM files are CardDemo's data; the screen, the COMMAREA, every EXEC DLI / CICS event and the final database are compared. Derived from CardDemo (Apache-2.0; Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): LICENSE and NOTICE here are the source's own.",
